      "transcriber_notes": [
        "Table printed sideways (rotated) on pp. 418-419 (Board of Trustees, parts I-III) and p. 420 (Executive Committee, on leaf p3-0035). The grand 'Total' printed at the foot of p. 419 covers parts I-III (Board of Trustees).",
        "Currency prefixes (NC $, US $) kept exactly where printed; unprefixed figures follow the currency of the figure above in the printed layout. Subtotal lines are unlabelled in the source; '[Subtotal NC]'/'[Subtotal US]' labels supplied by the transcriber.",
        "Part III: for items with 'Appropriated in NC$ / Appropriated in US $...' sub-lines, the breakdown figures are in an unheaded column printed left of Appropriation; the combined Appropriation/Payment/Reserved figures (printed level with the last sub-line) are placed on the item's heading row.",
        "Part III row 1 (National Geological Survey), Appropriation: printed 'NC$96,0?0.00' — the fourth digit is damaged (reads as 0 or 6); left blank. Reserve NC$8,000.00 and the part subtotal both imply 96,000.00.",
        "Total NC, Payment: printed 'NC$1,140,6?8.32' — the fifth digit is overprinted (5 or 3); left blank. Parts I-III payment subtotals (122,946.06 + 257,912.26 + 759,800.00) sum to 1,140,658.32.",
        "Figures printed with a comma as decimal separator kept as printed: '15,000,00' (III.3 appr.), '13,200,00' (III.5 pay.), '8,800,00' (III.8 pay.), '30,000,00' (III.14 pay.), '5,000,00' (III.18 appr.).",
        "Spellings kept as printed: 'Prizea' (I.4), 'Seceretary' (Exec. Comm. 6).",
        "Part I subtotals: NC appr. 50,000+28,800+37,000+10,000 = 125,800 — reconciles; US appr. 900+20,000+15,000 = 35,900 — reconciles (implies item 5 China Institute is in US $); NC payment 46,200+28,800+37,000+10,946.06 = 122,946.06 — reconciles; US payment 900+14,000+12,041.36 = 26,941.36 — reconciles; NC reserved 3,800+53.94 = 3,853.94 — reconciles; US reserved 600+2,958.64 = 3,558.64 — reconciles.",
        "Part II subtotals: appr. 135,000+5,000+50,000+80,000+10,000 = 280,000 — reconciles; payment 135,000+5,000+50,000+57,912.26+10,000 = 257,912.26 — reconciles.",
        "Part III subtotals: payments sum (excluding US $6,000 of item 20 and 5,000 of item 21) to 759,800 — reconciles only if item 21's 5,000.00 is US $ (the US subtotal 11,000 = 6,000 + 5,000 also implies this). Appropriations of items 2-21 excluding items 20 and 21 sum to 739,350; the printed NC$835,350 would require item 1 = 96,000 (the blank cell). Reserved 8,000+3,800+1,250+7,800+1,750+1,150+2,750+1,200+25,000+10,000+12,850 = 75,550 — reconciles. Breakdowns: 35,900+50,000=85,900; 8,700+6,250=14,950; 7,000+6,250=13,250; 8,000+25,000=33,000; 100,000+50,000=150,000; 50,000+93,750=143,750 — all reconcile.",
        "Grand totals (parts I-III): NC appr. 125,800+280,000+835,350 = 1,241,150 — reconciles; US appr. 35,900+11,000 = 46,900 — reconciles; US payment 26,941.36+11,000 = 37,941.36 — reconciles; NC reserved 3,853.94+75,550 = 79,403.94 — reconciles; US reserved 3,558.64 — reconciles.",
        "Executive Committee totals: NC appr. (items 1-11) 83,942.68, payment 48,939.52, reserved 35,003.16 — all reconcile; US appr. (items 12-14) 248.35+4,000+300 = 4,548.35, payment 106.79+2,000+300 = 2,406.79, reserved 141.56+1,041.36 = 1,182.92 — all reconcile (so items 13-14 are in US $). Note item 13: appr. 4,000.00 less payment 2,000.00 is 2,000.00, but reserve printed 1,041.36."
      ],
